Changes made on 2026-10-19
--------------------------
ApplePS2Controller.h retains DEBUGGER_SUPPORT=1 and every original field
and virtual declaration. VAIO_LEGACY_DEBUGGER_PATH=0 selects the ordinary
workloop keyboard interrupt/read path while retaining the original class
storage layout. No new member fields or virtual functions are introduced.

ApplePS2Controller.cpp initializes its existing resource pointers and flags,
uses OSMemberFunctionCast for three member event callbacks, and invokes the
new VAIOPS2Init.h from start() before workloop/client publication. The helper
uses bounded port I/O, a monotonic aggregate 20-second budget, separate
controller/device response handling, and explicit IRQ/clock/translation
readback. Long waits run with CPU interrupts enabled and without a spinlock.
Raw received bytes are logged only during cold initialization; request and
read-compare failures log command expectation/index/offline metadata without
received keyboard or mouse bytes. The controller emits the runtime marker
and publishes initialization results as IORegistry properties.

The cold-start experiment inhibits both ports, flushes bounded stale input,
reads a stable controller command byte, disables IRQs, tests both interfaces,
and resets the keyboard and mouse separately. Keyboard: FF -> FA -> AA,
F5 -> FA, EE -> EE. Mouse: D4 FF -> FA -> AA -> ID, D4 F6 -> FA,
D4 F5 -> FA. Only a received FE permits one resend. A timeout is never a
valid zero reply. Missing/nonzero port tests or a device handshake failure
are logged and may still permit the original plugin probes; persistently
busy/unsafe controller transport stops publication. At handoff, both clocks
are explicitly enabled, both IRQ-enable bits are clear, and translation is
set. The driver does not run controller AA self-test, write the output port,
alter A20, pulse system reset, change PCI/USB legacy registers, or use a
vendor-specific touchpad protocol. Existing runtime and power-management
logic otherwise remains the original Apple implementation; this work does
not claim to repair suspend/resume.

